From ecccc3ff49a5199f75f978ae21517e09ef764d3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:27:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc: run with umask 022 (ASUS's own commented-out line,
 switched on)

Every process rc starts inherits rc's umask, and with 0 a file created
without an explicit mode (fopen "w", a shell ">") was 0666 - writable by the
non-root services (dnsmasq and tftpd as nobody, Entware daemons) before root
read it back. Field report, GT-BE98.

The umask is set after sysinit's directory block, so every directory ASUS
creates 0777 on purpose keeps its stock mode. Services that must create files
as another user set their own (vsftpd local_umask, Samba force create mode,
tftpd -U, mkdir_if_none's -m 0777); chmod() ignores the umask, so every
explicit chmod is unchanged. test_rc_umask.py
---
 release/src/router/rc/init.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/init.c b/release/src/router/rc/init.c
index 43cec60dfd..7dd54a0aee 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/init.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/init.c
@@ -25640,7 +25640,18 @@ static void sysinit(void)
 	f_write("/etc/fstab", NULL, 0, 0, 0644);			// !!TB - blank
 	f_write("/tmp/settings", NULL, 0, 0, 0644);
 
-	//umask(022);
+	/* reaper 2026-10-09 (field report, GT-BE98): ASUS's own line, switched on.
+	 * Every process rc starts inherits rc's umask, and with 0 any file created
+	 * without an explicit mode (fopen "w", a shell ">") was 0666 - writable by
+	 * the non-root services (dnsmasq and tftpd as nobody, Entware daemons)
+	 * before root read it back. Placed here, after the directory block above,
+	 * so each directory ASUS made 0777 on purpose (/var/lock, /var/state,
+	 * /var/tmp/dhcp; /tmp is 01777) keeps exactly its stock mode. The services
+	 * that must create files as another user set their own: vsftpd
+	 * local_umask=000, Samba force create/directory mode 0777, tftpd's -U
+	 * default, mkdir_if_none's "mkdir -m 0777". chmod() ignores the umask, so
+	 * every explicit chmod in rc is unchanged. test_rc_umask.py */
+	umask(022);
 
 	if ((d = opendir("/rom/etc")) != NULL) {
 		while ((de = readdir(d)) != NULL) {
